#
# pce_prob, a block: four-valued probability from the paraconsistent
# decision engines (docs/PARACONSISTENT_ENGINES.md). A belief is a mass over
# TRUE, FALSE, BOTH and NEITHER given as four counts in that order, so
# conflict and ignorance are kept apart instead of averaged away.
zxblock 1
id       pce_prob
name     Paraconsistent probability
version  1.0.0
matrix 0
# Two independent sources joined on the knowledge order: TRUE from one and
# FALSE from the other lands on BOTH. Answers the joined mass, T F B N.
provides join num a b
logic    c join <<
prob.join
.
# A mass decided against thresholds th = decide_num decide_den
# conflict_num conflict_den: BOTH when the mass on BOTH reaches the
# conflict threshold, else TRUE or FALSE when that side reaches the decide
# threshold, NEITHER otherwise.
provides verdict truth m th
logic    c verdict <<
prob.verdict
.
# Exact Bayes: prior weights, likelihoods over den. Evidence every
# hypothesis calls impossible is refused, never divided by zero.
provides bayes num prior like den
logic    c bayes <<
prob.bayes
.
